# save: blank
# boot: power
# The regress boot (playtest/pt.py BOOT): START at frame 300 skips the APE logo straight to
# the quick title (FADE_IN(4,1) on NMIs), A at 501 fades the title out (FADE_OUT_WITH_MOSAIC
# (1,4,0)) into the file select menu; brightness compared on both fades (6e0e32bd)
# overclock: max
# compare: bright
# skip: 1
# skip: 2
# The quick title's graphics load runs across lag frames (310-311 merged): the NMI that would
# take FADE_IN's first delay tick ran before the call, so the original's fade-in reaches each
# step a logic frame later. In NMIs both step at the 2nd and every 2nd one after FADE_IN
# ignore: bright 312-319
# FILE_SELECT_INIT's FADE_IN(1,1) runs on NMIs during RUN_FILE_MENU's load lag in the original,
# so its ramp is 2-3 steps ahead of the port's and FILE_SELECT_MENU's @WAIT_FADE (a busy wait
# the emu counts as frames) ends 4 logic frames earlier; the port's last 4 wait frames have no
# counterpart
# ignore: bright 566-593
# extra: 594 595 596 597
---
300 -
1 START
200 -
1 A
400 -
